stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Idle

    Idle --> PromptRunning: Client sends prompt
    PromptRunning --> PromptRunning: Client answers request
    PromptRunning --> Finished: Turn ends or sees cancel
    Finished --> Idle: Next prompt starts

    PromptRunning --> AboutToAsk: Prompt decides to ask client
    AboutToAsk --> WaitingForClient: Request added (input open)
    WaitingForClient --> PromptRunning: Client answers request
    WaitingForClient --> Finished: Client cancels request

    PromptRunning --> ClosingSession: Client sends close or load
    AboutToAsk --> ClosingSession: Client sends close or load
    WaitingForClient --> ClosingSession: Client sends close or load
    ClosingSession --> Idle: Waiter cancelled and joined

    PromptRunning --> EofShuttingDown: Input hits EOF
    AboutToAsk --> EofShuttingDown: Input hits EOF
    WaitingForClient --> EofShuttingDown: Input hits EOF
    Idle --> EofShuttingDown: Input hits EOF

    EofShuttingDown --> EofReaping: Cancel existing waiters and close latch
    EofReaping --> Exited: Prompt thread exits (Design A & B)
    AboutToAsk --> HungWaiter: Current or unguarded begin adds open request
    EofReaping --> HungWaiter: Mutant b-no-loop misses late insert

    HungWaiter --> [*]: Breaks NoWaitAfterEof and BoundedExit
    Exited --> [*]

    note right of HungWaiter
        Shortest broken path (5 steps in current.cfg):
        Idle -> PromptRunning -> AboutToAsk -> ClosingSession (or EofReaping) -> HungWaiter
        Breaks NoWaitAfterEof (request stays open with no sweep) and BoundedExit.
    end note

    note right of AboutToAsk
        Design A: begin checks latch and session cancel under outbound_mutex,
        moving AboutToAsk directly to Finished on EOF or close/load.
        Design B: reap loops with bounded timeout D to re-sweep HungWaiter.
        Omitted from chart: session/cancel mid-turn (shares cancel path without
        closing input), mutant-cancel-latch (breaks ClientStillServed),
        and the non-atomic unlocked read state (merged into HungWaiter).
    end note
